 ### F2 (was C4). Capozziello, Lazkoz, Salzano, PRD 84, 124061 (2011), arXiv:1104.3096 (v1 and v2), Eq. (22): flat matter + CPL l₀, w_a² term missing a factor 9
 - **Printed:** l₀ = 35/2 + (1−Ω_m)/4·[213 + (7−Ω_m)w_a]w_a + … (typeset text, both arXiv versions; `runs/2026-10-30T0220Z/typeset/C4_*`, `runs/2026-10-30T0430Z/typeset/crop_v*p4-04.png`).
 - **Correct (model Eq. 17, E² = Ω_m(1+z)³ + (1−Ω_m)(1+z)^{3(1+w₀+w_a)}e^{−3w_a z/(1+z)}):** the bracket is [213 + 9(7−Ω_m)w_a], i.e. the w_a² term is (9/4)(1−Ω_m)(7−Ω_m)w_a². Printed − true = −2(1−Ω_m)(7−Ω_m)w_a². All other terms of (22), and q₀ (19), j₀ (20), are right; s₀ (21) is right once the missing "−" operator before 27/4 is supplied (the print has no operator there).
-- **Lean evidence (Checked):** `Checked.Cosmography.CPL.flatCPL_coeffs` (correct q₀, j₀, s₀, l₀ for every Ω, w₀, w_a; any scale factor obeying (17) near t₀, C⁵ at t₀); `printedL0_ne` (printed l₀ false in every such model with (1−Ω)(7−Ω)w_a ≠ 0); `clsL0Claim_false` (explicit model Ω = 0, w₀ = −1, w_a = 2/3, a = 1 − log(1−t): true 24, printed 160/9); `Checked.Cosmography.CPLExistence.exists_flatCPL`, `printedL0_false_at` (models exist for every parameter point, via Mathlib Picard–Lindelöf; so the printed l₀ is false at every point with (1−Ω)(7−Ω)w_a ≠ 0, e.g. the paper's own toy model (0.245[in✓F2_toy], −0.93[in✓F2_toy], −0.41[in✓F2_toy]): true 0.809[✓F2_toy(cosmoCoeff)], printed −0.906[✓F2_toy]). CI: see STATE.
+- **Lean evidence (Checked):** `Checked.Cosmography.CPL.flatCPL_coeffs` (correct q₀, j₀, s₀, l₀ for every Ω, w₀, w_a; any scale factor obeying (17) near t₀, C⁵ at t₀); `printedL0_ne` (printed l₀ false in every such model with (1−Ω)(7−Ω)w_a ≠ 0); `clsL0Claim_false` (explicit model Ω = 0, w₀ = −1, w_a = 2/3, a = 1 − log(1−t): true 24, printed 160/9); `Checked.Cosmography.CPLExistence.exists_flatCPL`, `printedL0_false_at` (models exist for every parameter point, via Mathlib Picard–Lindelöf; so the printed l₀ is false at every point with (1−Ω)(7−Ω)w_a ≠ 0, e.g. the paper's own toy model (0.245[in✓F2_toy], −0.41[in✓F2_toy], −0.93[in✓F2_toy]): true 0.809[✓F2_toy(cosmoCoeff)], printed −0.906[✓F2_toy]). CI: see STATE.
 - **Classification:** Source error (misprint). **Scope:** the paper's numbers are unaffected: its Fig. 2 (top) follows the correct l₀ (referee recomputed the residual curves; 3/4-parameter crossing at z ≈ 1.35[unc] correct vs 1.07[unc] printed; figure shows ≈ 1.35[src]), and its CPL inversions (Sec. VI, Models I–IV) use only Eqs. (19)–(21).
 - **Propagation:** the same formula with the missing 9 is reprinted in Bamba, Capozziello, Nojiri, Odintsov, Astrophys. Space Sci. 342, 155 (2012), arXiv:1205.3421, Eq. (11.38) (rendered page read: `runs/2026-10-30T0430Z/typeset/bamba_crop2.png`), a widely cited review. Anyone computing CPL l₀ from either formula with w_a ≠ 0 gets it wrong (e.g. Ω_m = 0.3[in✓F2_error], w_a = −0.5[in✓F2_error], any w₀: true − printed = 2(1−Ω_m)(7−Ω_m)w_a² = 2.345[✓F2_error]).
 - **Plain words:** one coefficient in a printed formula lost a factor 9; the authors' own plots used the right value, but the formula as printed (and as copied into a review) is wrong whenever the dark energy evolves (w_a ≠ 0).
